WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.399
Film Courage: How do you feel about the quote
“Never let your technique show?”

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:10.660
Houston Howard, Transmedia Author, Speaker
and Instructor: I think it’s a good quote.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:18.100
I think…skillful people, skillful people
at their craft, know how to do that well.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.100
I think

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.800
For example, I think story structure is great.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.119
I’m a big story structure nerd.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:28.220
I love [Robert] McKee and Syd Field, Blake
Snyder and all those guys.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.100
I love all that.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:35.980
Where story structure I think gets a bad rap
is when people use story structure but they

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.750
are not good enough to cover it up.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.870
And then they let the technique show.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:50.860
The great writers though I think use the structure
and they are good enough to weave such a tapestry

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.260
around that structure that it’s structured
but you don’t care, you don’t realize

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.760
that it’s there.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:02.989
That’s where I think the sweet spot it and
so in that regards I’m 100% in aggreeance

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:04.439
not to let the technique show.

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:13.770
I mean 
if you stripped everybody down to the bones,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.119
all of your skeletons will look pretty similar.

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:22.569
But the thing that makes us all unique is
when you start layering in all the different

00:01:22.569 --> 00:01:25.279
aspects of how we look even to the way we
dress.

00:01:25.279 --> 00:01:28.849
Once we add in all that stuff now we’re
all super unique and super different and super

00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:35.289
interesting and that is what I think makes
us individual people.

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:47.469
So people that let the technique show I think
struggle with executing in such a way to bury

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:49.560
it under their creative.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:55.079
I think people take that quote though to mean
that technique isn’t good.

00:01:55.079 --> 00:02:01.840
Like technique is somehow a bad thing that
technique is somehow this restrictive pejorative

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:09.079
kind of thing whether it is I think technique
gets a bad rap in that way.

00:02:09.079 --> 00:02:15.599
So I’m a huge advocate for strategy and
technique but the great creators (and this

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:21.860
is where the art comes in) is how do you use
the technique and use the structure and then

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:28.150
layer on top of that so much creativity and
such amazing ideas that people don’t see

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.819
it though it’s always there.

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:35.120
Film Courage: Somebody left a funny comment
on one of our videos and they said “Oh yeah,

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.370
your structure is great and you have the inciting
incident on this page…your script is horrible.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.459
But hey…great structure!”

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:49.640
Essentially making fun of if you don’t have
a great story then all of that is wasted.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.200
Houston: Sure.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.620
Entertainment is not paint-by-numbers and
that’s the variable, that will always be

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.849
the variable.

00:02:56.849 --> 00:03:03.080
Is that whether it’s Blake Snyder or Syd
Field or Robert McKee or whether you are doing

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:09.719
super story transmedia stuff like you can
have it all mapped out but the great variable

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:13.189
is are you good enough to execute?

00:03:13.189 --> 00:03:17.579
And yeah because technically your inciting
incident can be here and your Act 2 turning

00:03:17.579 --> 00:03:24.719
point is here and the dark-night-of-the-soul
is here and it’s all placed very well but

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:32.120
if you can’t execute in a way that makes
people forget about the technique then I think

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.560
it’s just a reflection on your talent or
maybe you just need to rewrite.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.900
Maybe you just need to take some more time
with it to be able to show your talent.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.430
That being said I think technique is necessary.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.689
Film Courage: Yes.

00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:48.550
Houston: And I think a lot of times people
throw the baby out with the bathwater so to

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.550
speak.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:54.189
And saying well story structure, we don’t
need that.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:58.530
It doesn’t matter where your inciting incident
is, it doesn’t matter if you have three

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.430
acts etcetera, etcetera.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.200
I don’t go that far at all.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.100
I think that stuff is necessary, you’ve
just got to be good enough to make people

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:05.119
forget about it.

